  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg">
        <tei:pb ed="1965" n="19" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg"/>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="90" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/1" n="1"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>The Prayer of Moses the man of God: Lord, Thou hast been a dwelling for us in every generation. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/2" n="2"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Before the mountains were born and Thou didst bring forth the earth and the world, from eternity to eternity Thou art God. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/3" n="3"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Thou dost restore mortals to contrition and say: Return, children of men. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/4" n="4"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>For a thousand years are in Thine eyes as a yesterday that passes and as a watch in the night. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/5" n="5"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Thou hast carried them off: they are in sleep; in the morning he is renewed like grass. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/6" n="6"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>In the morning it blossoms and is renewed, in the evening it withers and dries. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/7" n="7"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>For we are consumed through Thine anger and terrified through Thy wrath. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/8" n="8"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Thou hast placed our sins before Thee, our secret transgressions before the light of Thy countenance. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/9" n="9"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>For all our days pass away through Thine anger, we end our years like a fleeting thought. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/10" n="10"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>The days of our years — they are seventy years or, at full strength, eighty years, and their pride is toil and sorrow, since swiftly severed do we fly away. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/11" n="11"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Who knows the might of Thine anger and is Thy wrath according to the fear of Thee? <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/12" n="12"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>To count our days teach us well so that we may acquire a wise heart. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/13" n="13"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Turn again, O Lord — how much longer — and take pity on Thy servants. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/14" n="14"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Satisfy us in the morning with Thy grace that we may exult and rejoice all our days. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/15" n="15"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Cause us to rejoice as long as the days when Thou didst afflict us and the years when we saw misfortune. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/16" n="16"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>Let Thy work become apparent to Thy servants, and Thy splendour to their children; <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/90/17" n="17"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n54.jpg" n="19"/>and may the favour of the Lord our God be upon us; and firmly establish the work of our hands for us, the work of our hands, establish it firmly. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
